# A virtualenv built on the host. e2e/medallion/Dockerfile.pipeline runs
# `uv sync` and *then* copies the example directory over it, so a host .venv
# lands on top of the container's — macOS binaries in a Linux image, and the
# pipeline dies on `No module named 'requests'`. Anyone who follows the
# example's own README (`uv run python run_all.py`) has one; CI checks out
# fresh and never does, which is why this only bites contributors.
**/.venv
